0014: a mutable image without a format list keeps the tiling its compatibility class can describe.

**Status:** the behaviour is shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`; this text is the 23.11 one-decision
form, which is the A arm of the queue-16 A/B (`docs/release.md` provenance: the p14 binary was
built from an earlier text of this file). Upstream: not sent - the class is deliberately a
superset of the spec's, argued from the layout and not from a spec reading (ADR-0006).
**Found:** the inventory: 1983 MUTABLE-without-list creates, 3800.9 MiB of 7740.5 MiB sampled
(49.1 %), every one of them linear (`results/imginv-3variants.txt`, imginv4 row).

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. A stock driver answers a missing list with the worst case of "anything in the
class" and demotes the image to linear; here the class is enumerated, so an image whose class
describes one tiled layout keeps it. Compression is still dropped, which is the other question.

## Summary

With a `VkImageFormatListCreateInfo` the layout question is about that list. Without one the app
may view the image as anything in the compatibility class of the base format, and the stock
answer is linear. The patch synthesizes the class - same texel block (same bits per block, same
block shape), channel order still compared by the existing predicates, depth/stencil and
multi-planar excluded - and runs those predicates on it instead of on `NULL`. One function
decides: `tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear()` builds the class itself, and both callers
(the create and `tu_get_image_format_properties()`) ask it, so the two cannot disagree; the three
predicates go back to `static` because nothing outside `tu_formats.cc` calls them any more. The
UBWC predicate keeps seeing the application's list, never the class.

## Evidence

Hunks in `tu_formats.cc` (the enumerator, the single decision), `tu_formats.h` (one declaration
and its comment), `tu_image.cc` (the create asks the decision instead of comparing the predicates
itself). Measured by the queue-16 A/B of journal 40.29, which ran exactly this text as its A arm.

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| a no-list class keeps tiling | queue-16 A/B inventory, journal 40.29 | A 1450 creates / 2450.3 MiB tiled (60.0 %), B 0 MiB |
| the text is the measured behaviour | full test-suite log against the released stack, journal 33 | 0 of 598 lines differ (94-row matrix included) |
| the game's own creates | create signatures in both run logs, journal 36 | 784 signatures, 0 differing `tile=`/`ubwc=` |

## The change in this repo

It may only pull images out of linear. A list whose members really disagree (`{BGRA8, RGBA8}`,
NV12) must stay linear, and the UBWC predicate must keep the app's list. Revert: `git apply -R`
with the three file names explicit.

## Related

`0004` (refuses a linear sparse create), `0005`/`0006`/`0010` (the predicates it runs), `0013`
(the roundtrip it needs), ADR-0006; journal 40.29.

